-- A dipping cross-section of 20 x 10 cells over the gas cap, oil zone and
-- water zone of a three-component oil saturated at its gas-oil contact,
-- with SWATINIT, per-cell endpoints (SWL, SWCR, SGL, SGU) and rock
-- compressibility.  SWL rises with depth and down dip, SWCR lies 0.10 or
-- 0.12 above it, SGL is 0.02 in the down-dip half, and SGU is 1 - SWL.
--
-- Above the water-oil contact SWATINIT lies between SWL and SWCR, except in
-- columns 3 and 14, where it lies below SWL, and in the last eight metres
-- above the contact, where it rises to 0.75 and the water is mobile.  A
-- producer in column 8 draws from the oil zone and an injector in column 20
-- puts water into the water zone.  The compositional flow equations do not
-- include capillary pressure yet, so the mobile water above the contact is
-- not held in place.

